"- Object 1 Hazelnut\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A single, whole hazelnut with an intact, smooth outer shell and a visible, roughened base where the stem was attached.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The main body is a rich, warm reddish-brown with subtle variations in tone and faint lighter striations. The base is a darker, rougher brown with a fibrous texture.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Approximately 2.5 to 3 centimeters in length and 1.5 to 2 centimeters in width, typical of a mature hazelnut.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Hard, woody shell with a slightly glossy surface on the main body and a matte, fibrous texture at the base.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of a protective, lignified shell enclosing the edible seed inside; the shell is segmented and ridged, with a distinct basal scar.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One hazelnut.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned centrally in the frame, occupying the majority of the visual space.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The hazelnut is oriented with its pointed tip angled slightly upward and to the right, and its rounded base angled downward and to the left, viewed from a top-down perspective.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The base of the hazelnut shows a circular, roughened scar where the stem was once attached, indicating its botanical origin. No other attachments are present."